{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement the increment in Go as an extension of an existing channel configuration library (fabric-config style 'config' package), reusing its existing types and ConfigUpdate computation utilities rather than building a new library from scratch.",
    "Manipulate channel configuration through the Fabric protobuf types (common.Config, common.ConfigUpdate, common.ConfigUpdateEnvelope, msp.FabricMSPConfig) using proto marshal/unmarshal and protolator-style deep-copy semantics to avoid corrupting untouched config sections.",
    "Anchor peers (U1/U2/U7) are managed per organization via the org's AnchorPeers value; add/remove by host:port with idempotency checks (error on duplicate add, error on removing a non-existent peer).",
    "ConfigUpdate transactions are computed by diffing the original config against the modified config using the existing compute/diff helper, producing an envelope ready for the signature workflow.",
    "Certificate handling (U3/U4) uses Go crypto/x509 for parsing; U4 rejects certificates where IsCA is false or the KeyUsageCertSign key usage is missing; U3 appends the PEM-encoded revoked certificate to FabricMSPConfig.RevocationList for the target org's MSP.",
    "U8 exposes a getter returning a config.Orderer struct populated from the orderer configuration group so callers can mutate fields and pass the struct to the existing UpdateOrdererConfiguration function.",
    "Documentation examples (U5/U6) are implemented as Go testable examples (Example functions) so they appear in GoDoc and are compile-checked and executed by go test; U5 demonstrates multiple sequential updates plus signing of the ConfigUpdateEnvelope, U6 demonstrates building and signing a new channel creation transaction.",
    "Testing strategy: table-driven unit tests per function including negative paths (missing org, duplicate peer, invalid cert), plus example tests updated to demonstrate the new helpers (U7/U8)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A base channel configuration library already exists providing: channel config parsing/serialization, ConfigUpdate computation, config.Orderer type, UpdateOrdererConfiguration, and MSP/org group access helpers; this increment only adds the features in U1-U8.",
    "Development language is Go with the Hyperledger Fabric protobuf dependencies (fabric/protos-go or equivalent) already available in the module; target Fabric version is 1.4/2.x compatible.",
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates cover design, implementation, unit testing, example code, documentation, code review rework, and integration verification, but exclude release management, CI infrastructure changes, and deployment.",
    "Test fixtures (sample config blocks/transactions with multiple orgs, orderer config, and valid/invalid X.509 certificates) can be generated or reused from the existing repository test data.",
    "No changes to Hyperledger Fabric core or to other components are required; all work is confined to the library package and its tests/examples.",
    "Code review is performed asynchronously by a peer; only the review-rework time of the developer is included.",
    "Work-hours represent pure effort of one developer (not elapsed calendar time); an 8-hour workday is assumed only for context, not for scheduling."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and API design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze U1-U8, study the referenced channel update tutorial flow, and design the public API: function signatures for AddAnchorPeer, RemoveAnchorPeer, RevokeCertificate, AddRootCA, GetAnchorPeers, GetOrdererConfiguration; define error handling, validation rules, and how each operation feeds into ConfigUpdate computation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Environment setup and test fixture preparation",
      "activity_description": "Set up the development environment and prepare/extend test fixtures: base channel config blocks and transactions containing multiple orgs, orderer configuration, valid CA certificates, and invalid certificates (missing CA/KeyUsageCertSign) for negative tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement AddAnchorPeer",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to add an anchor peer (host/port) to a specified org's configuration, including duplicate detection, marshaling the updated AnchorPeers value, and verifying the resulting ConfigUpdate transaction is correctly computed and ready for signing. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2: Implement RemoveAnchorPeer",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to remove an anchor peer from a specified org's configuration, including handling of non-existent peers, updating the AnchorPeers value, and verifying ConfigUpdate computation. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement RevokeCertificate",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to revoke a certificate issued by an org's MSP by appending the certificate to the revocation_list attribute of the org's FabricMSPConfig and producing the corresponding configuration update. Includes unit tests covering target MSP selection and list modification.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U4: Implement AddRootCA with certificate validation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to add a root CA certificate to an MSP configuration, including x509 parsing and validation that rejects certificates missing the CA attribute or KeyUsageCertSign key usage, updating the MSP root certs list, and verifying ConfigUpdate computation. Includes positive and negative unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7: Implement GetAnchorPeers helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to retrieve existing anchor peers for a specific org without manual config parsing, including org-not-found handling; update the example test to demonstrate usage of this helper. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8: Implement GetOrdererConfiguration helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function to retrieve existing orderer configuration and return it as a config.Orderer value, verify the modify-then-update round trip with UpdateOrdererConfiguration, and update the example tests to demonstrate usage. Includes unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U5: GoDoc example for updating channel config and signing",
      "activity_description": "Write a testable GoDoc example demonstrating idiomatic usage for creating configuration updates involving multiple sequential changes (showing state management across updates) and signing the resulting ConfigUpdateEnvelope.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U6: GoDoc example for creating and signing channel creation transactions",
      "activity_description": "Write a testable GoDoc example demonstrating idiomatic usage for building a new channel creation transaction from scratch and signing it, suitable for display in the package GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration and regression verification",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end verification that all new operations produce valid ConfigUpdate transactions ready for the signature workflow (including against realistic config blocks), run the full library test suite to check for regressions, and fix any defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Code review rework, documentation polish, and finalization",
      "activity_description": "Address code review feedback, finalize GoDoc comments for all new exported functions, ensure linting/vetting passes, and prepare the increment for merge.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 114
  }
}

